<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Cyrene</h1><p class="st-meta">631 BCE – 440 BCE (approx.) · capital Cyrene</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Greek kingdom of the Battiad dynasty in eastern Libya, enriched by silphium, horses and grain.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, colonists from the island of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thera">Thera</a>, sent by the oracle of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delphi">Delphi</a>, founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> around 631 BCE under a leader who became King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battus-i-of-cyrene">Battus I</a>. The site, on a fertile plateau above the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a>, was shown to them by local <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/libu">Libyans</a>, with whom the settlers intermarried.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Eight kings, alternately named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battus-i-of-cyrene">Battus</a> and Arcesilaus, ruled for nearly two centuries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battus-ii-of-cyrene">Battus II</a> brought new settlers and defeated an Egyptian army sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apries">Apries</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-irasa">Irasa</a> around 570 BCE, and the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demonax-of-mantinea">Demonax of Mantinea</a> later limited royal power. The economy rested on silphium, a medicinal plant shown on the city's coins, and on horses and grain. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> from 525 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Royal power provoked repeated conflict, including Barca's secession. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcesilaus-iv">Arcesilaus IV</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> victory at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delphi">Delphi</a> in 462 BCE was celebrated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pindar">Pindar</a>, was overthrown around 440 BCE, and the monarchy gave way to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-cyrene">Republic of Cyrene</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 631 BCE – 440 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:47.14%;width:3.80%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>631 BCE – 440 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cyrene</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Battus I, Battus II, Arcesilaus IV</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Battiad Cyrene, Cyrene</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-536&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cyrene" aria-label="Kingdom of Cyrene on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5240 985 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Cyrene lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5560 1241L6140 1251M5560 1241L5560 1241M5560 1241L5536 1252"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1251h0M5560 1241h0M5536 1252h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5560 1241h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5560 1241h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cyrene. <a href="/atlas?year=-536&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cyrene">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
